Build Plan
This plan states the order in which the 49 apps should be built. It is designed so that each app can be built and tested using only the apps that already exist. No app requires a stub or a placeholder for an app that has not been built yet.

How the plan works
The plan is divided into stages. Each stage is a set of apps that can be built in parallel, because none of them depends on another app in the same stage.

A developer should build one app at a time, from Stage 1, then Stage 2, and so on. Each app is small. Each app has a complete specification. Each app can be tested on its own.

The dependency order is stated in the spec for each app. The plan below makes that order explicit.

Stage 1. The foundation
These apps have no dependencies. They can be built first, in any order.

App 12. N Calculator. The smallest app. No dependencies. Takes a target tail probability and a relative error, returns the required N. Build this first. It is the simplest test of the whole approach.

App 4. Scale-Separation Record Calculator. No dependencies. Takes two scales, their sources, and a band, returns a scale-separation record.

App 13. Gap-Score Reporter. No dependencies. Takes a dataset, candidate gaps, and an expected density, returns a table of Gap Scores.

App 17. STAG Schema Library. No dependencies. Packages the JSON Schema, the SHACL schema, the 32 semantic rules, and the codebook.

App 18. Null-Model Protocol Library. No dependencies. Packages the statistic, the scan families, the effective-null builder, and the full-pipeline simulator as a library.

App 22. Numerical Verification Tool. No dependencies. Takes a document and a source list, returns a verification table.

App 49. Autofill Library Service. No dependencies. Provides autofill for every other app.

