What to tell a developer
If a developer asks "where do I start," the answer is: App 12, the N Calculator. It is the smallest app, it has no dependencies, and it is the quickest win. If App 12 works, the whole approach is proven, and the developer can move to App 4, then App 13.

If a developer asks "can I build App 9," the answer is: not yet. App 9 depends on App 18, App 11, and App 12. Those have to exist first. If the developer wants to build App 9, they should build App 12 first, then App 18, then App 11, then App 9.

If a developer asks "can I build the Master Workbench," the answer is: no. It depends on everything else. It is the last thing to build.

The one-line version
Build the foundation first. Then the annotation and statistics layers. Then the storage and combination layers. Then the domain registries. Then the meta-level tools. Then the orchestrator. One app at a time. Each app is small. Each app has a complete specification.

